  "goodToKnow": "Die Kalorie is a calorie: Kalorien zählen, kalorienarm (low-calorie), kalorienreich (high-calorie). On German food labels, energy is given in both kcal and kJ (Kilojoule), per 100 grams, under Nährwerte. Colloquially, people talk about Kalorien when they mean kilocalories. Stress the last syllable: ka-lo-REE, and in the plural ka-lo-REE-en. From Latin calor, heat."
